00:41:59.490 --> 00:42:02.430
non-jazz competing
a capella group.

00:42:02.430 --> 00:42:04.100
So that makes this special.

00:42:04.100 --> 00:42:05.989
And you're all special too.

00:42:05.989 --> 00:42:07.530
We're going to sing
another song now.

00:42:07.530 --> 00:42:10.350
THE COROLLARIES: (SINGING)
We are the engineers.

00:42:10.350 --> 00:42:17.775
We are the engineers.

00:42:17.775 --> 00:42:19.950
Yes, we are the engineers.

00:42:19.950 --> 00:42:22.410
TSIEN: So you shouldn't
think that MIT

00:42:22.410 --> 00:42:24.570
has no art, because
they've got them

00:42:24.570 --> 00:42:27.060
sprawling all over the place.

00:42:27.060 --> 00:42:29.910
BRODY: Well, now, the advice
I give to incoming freshmen

00:42:29.910 --> 00:42:34.660
consistently is don't
leave your trumpet at home.

00:42:34.660 --> 00:42:35.600
You can use it here.

00:42:38.360 --> 00:42:40.210
MCGANN: So we've
got a live check-in

00:42:40.210 --> 00:42:44.770
over at Johnson Athletic Center,
where the graduates are busily

00:42:44.770 --> 00:42:48.020
getting ready for
their walk over here.

00:42:48.020 --> 00:42:49.090
So can you see?

00:42:49.090 --> 00:42:52.510
Can you find your
graduate out there?

00:42:52.510 --> 00:42:56.860
Right now, while MIT students
are, in the long-term, focused

00:42:56.860 --> 00:43:00.130
on that mission of MIT
to change the world,

00:43:00.130 --> 00:43:02.230
to make the world a
better place, right now,

00:43:02.230 --> 00:43:05.980
their mission, I think, is
just to get in that snack line,

00:43:05.980 --> 00:43:08.840
grab some muffins
and orange juice.

00:43:08.840 --> 00:43:11.348
Now, you should know
that at MIT, there are--

00:43:14.160 --> 00:43:18.130
there are no classes that
really begin before 10:00 AM.

00:43:18.130 --> 00:43:21.100
So this is extremely
early for MIT students.

00:43:21.100 --> 00:43:24.190
So you can see a lot of
sleepy students in line.

00:43:24.190 --> 00:43:27.460
But they're very excited to
