00:43:27.460 --> 00:43:29.420
and sitting in these
black seats in front of us

00:43:29.420 --> 00:43:31.210
not very long from now.

00:43:31.210 --> 00:43:33.730
So right now, what
we're going to do

00:43:33.730 --> 00:43:36.670
is-- we just saw in a video
about the arts at MIT.

00:43:36.670 --> 00:43:39.790
Now, we're going to throw
it to a ZigZag piece looking

00:43:39.790 --> 00:43:41.830
at other activities at MIT.

00:43:41.830 --> 00:43:44.380
MIT has just a
plethora of activities,

00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:47.740
more than 330 different student
groups, 41 varsity sports.

00:43:47.740 --> 00:43:48.682
There's so much to do.

00:43:48.682 --> 00:43:50.140
Why don't you check
this piece out?

00:43:50.140 --> 00:43:54.158
It's really quite interesting.

00:43:54.158 --> 00:43:57.260
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:43:59.180 --> 00:44:01.852
Coming to you from the Johnson
Athletic Center at MIT,

00:44:01.852 --> 00:44:02.810
My name is Matt McGann.

00:44:02.810 --> 00:44:05.330
And this is ZigZag, now
available in high-definition.

00:44:05.330 --> 00:44:08.864
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:44:12.330 --> 00:44:14.240
At most campuses
across the country,

00:44:14.240 --> 00:44:17.570
athletics are an integral part
of the college experience.

00:44:17.570 --> 00:44:20.390
At MIT, students apply
the same passion, drive,

00:44:20.390 --> 00:44:25.280
and commitment to athletics
as they do academics.

00:44:25.280 --> 00:44:28.370
The Institute fields
41 NCAA teams,

00:44:28.370 --> 00:44:31.110
as many as any other
school in the nation.

00:44:31.110 --> 00:44:35.090
But when it comes to athletics,
the key word is participation.

00:44:35.090 --> 00:44:37.760
More than 10,000 members
of the MIT community

00:44:37.760 --> 00:44:41.660
participate every year in a rich
and varied intramural program.

00:44:41.660 --> 00:44:44.540
At MIT, students would
rather be on the field

00:44:44.540 --> 00:44:45.549
than in the stands.

00:44:45.549 --> 00:44:47.090
ANDERSON: One of
the reasons I really

00:44:47.090 --> 00:44:52.040
enjoy working here at MIT is
because our student athletes

00:44:52.040 --> 00:44:54.860
don't have to sacrifice
their academics for athletics

00:44:54.860 --> 00:44:56.120
and vice-versa.

00:44:56.120 --> 00:44:57.680
We want our student
athletes here

00:44:57.680 --> 00:45:01.030
to do just what that term says.

00:45:01.030 --> 00:45:03.640
You're a student first,
and you're an athlete next.

00:45:03.640 --> 00:45:08.470
On an annual basis,
we get 760,000 visits

00:45:08.470 --> 00:45:10.700
in our recreation department.

00:45:10.700 --> 00:45:14.240
And our varsity sports, I
think that speaks for itself.

00:45:14.240 --> 00:45:15.830
We have 41 varsity sports.

00:45:15.830 --> 00:45:18.500
And we're tied with
Harvard for the most

00:45:18.500 --> 00:45:21.110
sports at any institution
of higher learning.

00:45:21.110 --> 00:45:25.010
The breadth and depth of our
program is an inclusive one.

00:45:25.010 --> 00:45:27.080
We have 29 clubs.

00:45:27.080 --> 00:45:29.610
We have a strong
intramural sports program.

00:45:29.610 --> 00:45:33.680
You take a PE class, for
instance, our students may come

00:45:33.680 --> 00:45:35.310
here and never skated before.

00:45:35.310 --> 00:45:36.720
They put on a pair of skates.

00:45:36.720 --> 00:45:38.140
And they learn to skate.

00:45:38.140 --> 00:45:41.140
And two months later, they're
playing in an ice hockey game.

00:45:41.140 --> 00:45:42.470
That's just unreal to me.

00:45:42.470 --> 00:45:45.130
But the MIT students, they want
to be excellent at everything

00:45:45.130 --> 00:45:45.630
they do.

00:45:45.630 --> 00:45:47.994
So it doesn't surprise me
at all to see that happen.

00:45:47.994 --> 00:45:49.410
And it happens on
a regular basis.

00:45:49.410 --> 00:45:52.460
Our student athletes, when we
get a chance to work with them,

00:45:52.460 --> 00:45:53.900
they learn leadership.

00:45:53.900 --> 00:45:55.940
They learn to work as a team.

00:45:55.940 --> 00:45:59.240
They learn that they can push
themselves beyond whatever

00:45:59.240 --> 00:46:00.740
thought they could do.

00:46:00.740 --> 00:46:02.769
They learn to take charge
without taking over.

00:46:02.769 --> 00:46:04.310
And these are the
same kind of skills

00:46:04.310 --> 00:46:06.470
that you can take
from the playing field

00:46:06.470 --> 00:46:09.696
and get to the boardroom,
and you can use those there.

00:46:09.696 --> 00:46:11.570
We know that they are
really, really prepared

00:46:11.570 --> 00:46:14.028
when they move to the next
game, which is the game of life.

00:46:14.028 --> 00:46:16.920
MCGANN: MIT fields more than
2,000 intramural sports teams

00:46:16.920 --> 00:46:18.740
and nearly two dozen sports.

00:46:18.740 --> 00:46:21.680
And 80% of MIT students
participate in some form

00:46:21.680 --> 00:46:23.000
of organized athletics.

00:46:29.060 --> 00:46:31.720
We all know that MIT is renowned
