00:55:57.760 --> 00:55:59.730
Well, our video
magazine, ZigZag,

00:55:59.730 --> 00:56:02.790
is just one example of the rich
assortment of video content

00:56:02.790 --> 00:56:04.950
that's available on the web.

00:56:04.950 --> 00:56:07.806
The explosive
popularity of YouTube

00:56:07.806 --> 00:56:09.180
demonstrates that
people not only

00:56:09.180 --> 00:56:11.190
want to watch video
of their choosing

00:56:11.190 --> 00:56:14.850
but also to create and
share their own content.

00:56:14.850 --> 00:56:17.940
MIT recently launched its
own version of YouTube,

00:56:17.940 --> 00:56:22.180
which is called MIT Tech TV.

00:56:22.180 --> 00:56:25.400
This site will allow for the MIT
community, including students,

00:56:25.400 --> 00:56:28.540
faculty, and staff,
to upload, view,

00:56:28.540 --> 00:56:30.910
and share quality
science, engineering,

00:56:30.910 --> 00:56:34.750
and MIT-related content,
providing a global audience

00:56:34.750 --> 00:56:36.850
with a window into MIT.

00:56:36.850 --> 00:56:39.460
It will not surprise you to
know that many of our students

00:56:39.460 --> 00:56:42.670
are also talented media
producers, as evidenced

00:56:42.670 --> 00:56:45.790
by these two pieces submitted
to the student video

00:56:45.790 --> 00:56:49.240
contest sponsored by the Dean
of the School of Engineering.

00:56:49.240 --> 00:56:51.451
Let's check it out.

