One of the main
technological challenges

01:04:52.730 --> 01:04:55.400
to the widespread use
of electric vehicles

01:04:55.400 --> 01:04:57.240
is limited battery life.

01:04:57.240 --> 01:05:00.290
But at MIT'S Laboratory for
Electromagnetic and Electronic

01:05:00.290 --> 01:05:03.770
Systems, new research is
promising a viable alternative

01:05:03.770 --> 01:05:06.420
to conventional batteries,
the ultra capacitor.

01:05:06.420 --> 01:05:08.960
SCHINDALL: Research is
fascinating in that you often

01:05:08.960 --> 01:05:11.930
end up doing something you
never expected to be doing.

01:05:11.930 --> 01:05:13.860
We start with the
basic capacitor.

01:05:13.860 --> 01:05:15.650
They're very, very
effective in that you

01:05:15.650 --> 01:05:18.030
can charge and discharge
them indefinitely.

01:05:18.030 --> 01:05:20.090
They store energy
just like a battery.

01:05:20.090 --> 01:05:24.020
But they store much less energy
than a battery does, not enough

01:05:24.020 --> 01:05:26.230
to be useful in
electronic devices.

01:05:26.230 --> 01:05:28.760
Now, an ultra capacitor
is a great improvement

01:05:28.760 --> 01:05:30.800
over an ordinary capacitor.

01:05:30.800 --> 01:05:35.540
An ultra capacitor has about
1/25 the energy of a battery.

01:05:35.540 --> 01:05:38.270
We were simply looking
at ultra capacitors

01:05:38.270 --> 01:05:42.140
to see if they would be useful
to automobile manufacturers.

01:05:42.140 --> 01:05:44.990
And we made the
connection that perhaps we

01:05:44.990 --> 01:05:48.740
could take an old
product, a capacitor,

01:05:48.740 --> 01:05:52.130
and make that old
product in a new way,

01:05:52.130 --> 01:05:55.130
use a new technology,
nanotechnology,

01:05:55.130 --> 01:05:59.270
or a nanotube technology,
and actually build

01:05:59.270 --> 01:06:01.220
a product that is
better than what's

01:06:01.220 --> 01:06:04.960
out there before at a
cost-effective price.

01:06:04.960 --> 01:06:08.330
What we're doing is
taking a capacitor

01:06:08.330 --> 01:06:11.180
and coating the plates
of the capacitor

01:06:11.180 --> 01:06:14.500
with hair-like
nanotubes growing out

01:06:14.500 --> 01:06:16.640
from the surface of
the capacitor plates.

01:06:16.640 --> 01:06:19.580
The ions, which store
the electrical charge,

01:06:19.580 --> 01:06:23.060
are attracted into the
spaces between the nanotubes,

01:06:23.060 --> 01:06:26.330
allowing the capacitor to store
an amount of energy that's

01:06:26.330 --> 01:06:29.840
comparable to what is
ordinarily stored by a battery.

01:06:29.840 --> 01:06:31.820
That would be a
significant improvement

01:06:31.820 --> 01:06:35.930
with many, many applications,
ranging from small devices that

01:06:35.930 --> 01:06:39.050
could be more quickly
recharged to larger devices,

01:06:39.050 --> 01:06:42.890
such as automobiles, where the
braking energy can be captured

01:06:42.890 --> 01:06:44.930
in one of these devices.

01:06:44.930 --> 01:06:48.380
And that braking energy can then
be used to accelerate the car

01:06:48.380 --> 01:06:51.047
and make the overall
operation of the automobile

01:06:51.047 --> 01:06:52.130
much, much more efficient.

