04:56:36.720 --> 04:56:38.898
[READING NAMES]

04:56:53.335 --> 04:56:55.780
Doctor of Philosophy with
all the rights and privileges

04:56:55.780 --> 04:56:57.190
pertaining thereto.

04:56:57.190 --> 04:56:59.386
[READING NAMES]

04:58:40.990 --> 04:58:44.982
MEAD: Congratulations to all
of the graduates of 2007.

04:58:56.540 --> 04:58:58.320
It's now my pleasure
to introduce

04:58:58.320 --> 04:59:03.480
Martin Tang, the Chief Marshal
who will greet the graduates.

04:59:03.480 --> 04:59:07.620
Mr. Tang is a member
of the class of 1972,

04:59:07.620 --> 04:59:11.974
and is currently serving as the
president of the Association

04:59:11.974 --> 04:59:14.920
of Alumni and Alumnae of MIT.

04:59:14.920 --> 04:59:15.902
Martin, please.

04:59:23.714 --> 04:59:24.630
TANG: Thank you, Dana.

04:59:24.630 --> 04:59:26.960
Good afternoon, all.

04:59:26.960 --> 04:59:29.190
It it's my honor to
recognize the distinguished

04:59:29.190 --> 04:59:34.980
class of 2007, the
newest alumni of MIT.

04:59:34.980 --> 04:59:40.490
The entire alumni body,
now some 118,000 strong,

04:59:40.490 --> 04:59:45.090
joins me in congratulating
all of the 2007 graduates,

04:59:45.090 --> 04:59:48.150
and officially welcoming
you into the alumni

04:59:48.150 --> 04:59:51.090
family, your infinite
connection to MIT.

04:59:51.090 --> 04:59:52.070
Thank you.

05:00:06.790 --> 05:00:10.780
MEAD: The 141st
commencement exercises

05:00:10.780 --> 05:00:14.748
of the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology

05:00:14.748 --> 05:00:16.236
are now concluded.

05:00:26.170 --> 05:00:30.590
A reception will now follow on
Kresge Oval on the West Campus

05:00:30.590 --> 05:00:32.160
plaza.

05:00:32.160 --> 05:00:36.820
And at this time, will the
stage assembly and the audience

05:00:36.820 --> 05:00:40.205
please rise and join
the MIT Chorallaries

05:00:40.205 --> 05:00:43.151
in singing the school song.

05:00:46.097 --> 05:00:50.025
[MUSIC PLAYING]

05:00:56.930 --> 05:01:03.570
MIT CHORALLARIES (SINGING):
Arise all ye of MIT,

05:01:03.570 --> 05:01:07.070
in loyal fellowship.

05:01:09.710 --> 05:01:21.970
The future beckons unto ye
and life is full and rich.

05:01:21.970 --> 05:01:28.644
Arise and raise
your glass on high;

05:01:28.644 --> 05:01:37.599
tonight shall ever
be a memory that

05:01:37.599 --> 05:01:43.524
will never die for ye of MIT.

05:01:46.870 --> 05:01:59.580
Thy sons and daughters, MIT,
return from far and wide

05:01:59.580 --> 05:02:11.942
and gather here once more to
be renourished by thy side,

05:02:11.942 --> 05:02:24.615
and as we raise our glasses high
to pledge our love for thee,

05:02:24.615 --> 05:02:33.938
we join all those of days
gone by in praise of MIT.

05:02:40.412 --> 05:02:45.360
Oh, I wish that I were
back again at Tech

05:02:45.360 --> 05:02:48.020
on Boylston Street,
dressed in my dinky uniform

05:02:48.020 --> 05:02:50.060
so dapper and so neat.

05:02:50.060 --> 05:02:53.248
I'm crazy after calculus,
I never had enough;

05:02:53.248 --> 05:02:55.268
so it's hard to be
dragged away so young,

05:02:55.268 --> 05:02:57.060
it was horribly awfully tough!

05:02:57.060 --> 05:02:59.670
Hurrah for technology,
'ology, 'ology,

05:02:59.670 --> 05:03:03.992
oh, glorious old technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh!

05:03:03.992 --> 05:03:05.700
Back in the days that
were free from care

05:03:05.700 --> 05:03:09.390
in the 'ology varsity shop, with
nothing to do but analyze air

05:03:09.390 --> 05:03:10.650
in an anemometrical top.

05:03:10.650 --> 05:03:14.090
The differentiation of
the trigonometric powers,

05:03:14.090 --> 05:03:16.020
the constant pi
that made me sigh

05:03:16.020 --> 05:03:17.390
in those happy days of ours.

05:03:17.390 --> 05:03:20.330
Hurrah for technology,
'ology, 'ology,

05:03:20.330 --> 05:03:24.666
oh, glorious old technology,
'ology, 'ology, oh!

05:03:24.666 --> 05:03:27.926
Take me back on a special train
to that glorious institute,

05:03:27.926 --> 05:03:31.410
I yearn for the inspiration
of a technological toot.

05:03:31.410 --> 05:03:34.982
I'd shun the quizzical physical
profs, the chapel and all that,

05:03:34.982 --> 05:03:38.426
but how I'd love to go
again on a scientific bat.

05:03:38.426 --> 05:03:43.346
La-la la-la, la-la la-la,
la-la-la la-la la la, la-la la

05:03:43.346 --> 05:03:44.330
la.

05:03:44.330 --> 05:03:45.314
La-la la-la.

05:03:45.314 --> 05:03:46.290
Da, da-da-da!

05:03:46.290 --> 05:03:46.790
La-la-la.

05:03:46.790 --> 05:03:47.774
Da da.

05:03:47.774 --> 05:03:50.760
Da-da, da-da, da-da, da-da!

05:03:50.760 --> 05:03:58.626
Oh, M-A-S-S-A-C-H-U-S-E-T-T-S,
I-N-S-T-I-T-U-T-E O-F T-E.

05:03:58.626 --> 05:04:05.204
And then it's C-H-N-O-L-O-G
and Y comes after G,

05:04:05.204 --> 05:04:09.195
it's the Massachusetts
Institute of Technology!

05:04:09.195 --> 05:04:09.695
Hey!

05:04:15.683 --> 05:04:20.174
[MUSIC PLAYING]

05:07:06.840 --> 05:07:10.832
[MUSIC PLAYING]

05:09:45.522 --> 05:09:50.764
[MUSIC PLAYING]

